n\'t available, maybe the pod has crashed and the logs have been lost, which would require checking the events or the deployment configuration.\n\nAlternatively, if the logs don\'t show anything, we might need to check the pod\'s events using "kubectl describe pod" to see if there are any events related to the pod\'s failure, such as image pull errors, startup failures, or resource issues. But since the user has a limited number of tool calls, it\'s best to first check the logs, as that\'s the most direct way to see what\'s going wrong.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The "geo" pod is in an "Error" state with 3 restarts. To diagnose the root cause, I need to retrieve its logs to identify specific errors (e.g., crashes, configuration issues, or dependency failures). The pod name "geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5" was identified in the previous step, so I will use it to fetch logs. This will provide critical insights into why the pod is failing.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 516, 'prompt_tokens': 3263, 'total_tokens': 3779, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb38-94d3-72f2-b281-accbe383d475-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3263, 'output_tokens': 516, 'total_tokens': 3779}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4254120c-c782-4f0a-8c51-0f91dba4c160'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose the "geo" service in the hotel-reservation application. From the previous steps, we know that the "geo" deployment has 0/1 pods running, and the specific pod "geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5" is in an Error state with 3 restarts. The next logical step is to check the logs of that pod to find out why it\'s failing.\n\nThe available tools include the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, which allows running kubectl commands. The user already tried getting the logs but got an error because the pod name was incorrect. Wait, no—the previous attempt to get logs used "geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x", which didn\'t exist, leading to a Not Found error. Then, when they ran "kubectl get pods", they found the correct pod name: "geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5". \n\nSo now, the correct pod name is known. The next tool call should be to get the logs for that specific pod. The command would be "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5 -n hotel-reservation". This will retrieve the logs, which can help identify the root cause of the Error state. The logs might show crashes, configuration issues, missing dependencies, or other errors that are causing the pod to fail repeatedly. \n\nTherefore, using the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the correct pod name and namespace should provide the necessary information to diagnose the problem. There\'s no need for other tools right now since the logs are the most direct way to see what\'s wrong with the pod.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5 -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8e68839bfc59a1e7', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 408, 'prompt_tokens': 4276, 'total_tokens': 4684, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb38-acf2-7793-bd76-58f3db9eeb78-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5 -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8e68839bfc59a1e7', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4276, 'output_tokens': 408, 'total_tokens': 4684}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T09:55:12Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T09:55:12Z","message":"Set global log level: info"}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T09:55:12Z","message":"Tune: setGCPercent to 100"}\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T09:55:12Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/geo/main.go:23\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mReading config...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T09:55:12Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/geo/main.go:36\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mRead database URL: mongodb-geo:27017\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T09:55:12Z\x1b[0m \x1b[32mINF\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/geo/main.go:37\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mInitializing DB connection...\x1b[0m\n\x1b[90m2026-03-17T09:55:12Z\x1b[0m \x1b[31mPNC\x1b[0m \x1b[1mcmd/geo/db.go:26\x1b[0m\x1b[36m >\x1b[0m \x1b[1mserver returned error on SASL authentication step: Authentication failed.\x1b[0m\npanic: server returned error on SASL authentication step: Authentication failed.\n\ngoroutine 1 [running]:\ngithub.com/rs/zerolog.(*Logger).Panic.func1({0xc000170000, 0x0})\n\t/go/src/github.com/harlow/go-micro-services/vendor/github.com/rs/zerolog/log.go:405 +0x2d\ngithub.com/rs/zerolog.(*Event).msg(0xc000158070, {0xc000170000, 0x49})\n\t/go/src/github.com/harlow/go-micro-services/vendor/github.com/rs/zerolog/event.go:158 +0x2b8\ngithub.com/rs/zerolog.(*Event).Msg(...)\n\t/go/src/github.com/harlow/go-micro-services/vendor/github.com/rs/zerolog/event.go:110\nmain.initializeDatabase({0xc0001c81e0, 0xc00019bdd0})\n\t/go/src/github.com/harlow/go-micro-services/cmd/geo/db.go:26 +0x167\nmain.main()\n\t/go/src/github.com/harlow/go-micro-services/cmd/geo/main.go:38 +0x877\n', id='ca297a72-d730-48c8-aaf6-c3fd0a4aadae', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-8e68839bfc59a1e7'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a53fdab0-1d1e-405b-bb79-83803f97f0b3')]]
