}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 284, 'prompt_tokens': 2361, 'total_tokens': 2645, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb38-758a-7082-8e6b-5fa9d317480d-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2361, 'output_tokens': 284, 'total_tokens': 2645}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='bb87e72f-5ffd-4f0b-87b4-cdbd0b307a49'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the "geo" service in the hotel-reservation namespace isn\'t ready. Previously, they tried to get the logs of the pod "geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x" but got a "NotFound" error. That means the pod doesn\'t exist or isn\'t running.\n\nSo, the next step should be to check the list of all pods in the namespace to see the current state. The command "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation" will show if there are any pods associated with the "geo" deployment. If the pod isn\'t listed, maybe it\'s in a pending state or there\'s an issue with the deployment configuration. \n\nLooking at the previous output from "kubectl get deployments", the "geo" deployment has 0/1 replicas ready. That suggests that the deployment isn\'t successfully creating pods. By checking the pods list, we can confirm if the pod is missing, if there are any errors, or if there\'s a problem with the node scheduling. \n\nOnce we have the pod list, we can then proceed to check the deployment details, describe the pod, or look into events related to the deployment. But first, verifying the existence and status of the pod is crucial. So, using "kubectl get pods" in the specified namespace makes sense here.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-872d5413a475284f', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 316, 'prompt_tokens': 3368, 'total_tokens': 3684, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb38-8324-7f43-a436-8a370985ba95-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-872d5413a475284f', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3368, 'output_tokens': 316, 'total_tokens': 3684}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                                      READY   STATUS    RESTARTS       AGE\nconsul-5c696cc4dc-xzw4t                   1/1     Running   0              2m23s\nfrontend-6df8475df4-422qr                 1/1     Running   0              2m23s\ngeo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5                      0/1     Error     3 (30s ago)    52s\njaeger-5b9775bd94-2t8ms                   1/1     Running   0              2m21s\nmemcached-profile-6849578b8-6d246         1/1     Running   0              2m20s\nmemcached-rate-948594dfd-lldlc            1/1     Running   0              2m19s\nmemcached-reserve-68dbb57476-7gd2z        1/1     Running   0              2m15s\nmongodb-geo-8cb7d9f5b-ppbms               1/1     Running   0              2m22s\nmongodb-profile-775dfd4bd7-zk6wz          1/1     Running   0              2m20s\nmongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-zf8j6              1/1     Running   0              2m18s\nmongodb-recommendation-674dddbcdf-29c9r   1/1     Running   0              2m17s\nmongodb-reservation-6cdf69dcc-j4c5t       1/1     Running   0              2m14s\nmongodb-user-6dcf4877-8lmwz               1/1     Running   0              2m9s\nprofile-69