is in an Error state with 3 restarts. The next logical step is to check the logs of that pod to find out why it\'s failing.\n\nThe available tools include the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd, which allows running kubectl commands. The user already tried getting the logs but got an error because the pod name was incorrect. Wait, no—the previous attempt to get logs used "geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x", which didn\'t exist, leading to a Not Found error. Then, when they ran "kubectl get pods", they found the correct pod name: "geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5". \n\nSo now, the correct pod name is known. The next tool call should be to get the logs for that specific pod. The command would be "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5 -n hotel-reservation". This will retrieve the logs, which can help identify the root cause of the Error state. The logs might show crashes, configuration issues, missing dependencies, or other errors that are causing the pod to fail repeatedly. \n\nTherefore, using the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the correct pod name and namespace should provide the necessary information to diagnose the problem. There\'s no need for other tools right now since the logs are the most direct way to see what\'s wrong with the pod.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5 -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8e68839bfc59a1e7', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 408, 'prompt_tokens': 4276, 'total_tokens': 4684, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb38-acf2-7793-bd76-58f3db9eeb78-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5 -n h