 to get a summary of its status, events, and any errors. However, the logs would be more direct for seeing runtime errors. \n\nSo, the next tool call should be to get the logs of the "geo" pod. The command would be `kubectl logs geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x -n hotel-reservation`. Alternatively, if the pod name isn\'t known, they might need to first get the pod name. But since the user already has the pod name from the previous output, they can directly access the logs. \n\nAnother possibility is to check the metrics using Prometheus to see if there are any resource issues like CPU or memory limits being exceeded. But given that the deployment is not ready, checking the logs is more immediate. \n\nTherefore, the next step is to retrieve the logs of the "geo" pod to identify the root cause of the failure.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a5a2f0a477741ebe', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 679, 'prompt_tokens': 3113, 'total_tokens': 3792, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb38-5348-7a83-983b-890822300261-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a5a2f0a477741ebe', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3113, 'output_tokens': 679, 'total_tokens': 3792}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl command:\nerror: error from server (NotFound): pods "geo-7df5888d64-2qk4x" not found in namespace "hotel-reservation"\n', id='36a68f57-f67c-4296-935c-dab9d450e1e2', 