 the connection would fail. The user might need to verify the MongoDB service\'s endpoint and ensure the application is connecting to the correct address.\n\nSince the logs point to an authentication failure, the next step is to verify the Secret\'s contents and the environment variables being used. The user can check the Secret\'s data to ensure the keys and values are correct. Then, confirm that the Deployment is correctly referencing those keys. If everything looks right, maybe the MongoDB instance itself has issues, like the user not having the right permissions or the database not being up.\n\nThe user should also check the MongoDB pod\'s logs to see if there are any errors related to the connection attempts. If the MongoDB service is down or not accepting connections, that would also cause authentication failures. So, verifying the status of the MongoDB pod and its logs would be another step.\n\nIn summary, the immediate next action is to check the Secret\'s data and the Deployment\'s environment variable references. If those are correct, then investigate the MongoDB service\'s status and configuration.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod -n hotel-reservation geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b5dc796d486f6b77', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 574, 'prompt_tokens': 5650, 'total_tokens': 6224, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb3a-a816-7211-a265-5744ac662fec-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod -n hotel-reservation geo-57c7bd6d5c-p6fr5'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b5dc796d486f6b77', 'type': 'tool_call'}], inval