 they can restart the pod or rollout the deployment to apply the changes. Finally, they should verify the pod\'s status to ensure it\'s running without errors.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \nreasoning: Verify that the `mongodb-geo-auth` Secret is correctly referenced in the `geo` service\'s deployment configuration. This ensures the Secret is mounted as a volume or environment variable in the `geo` pod, allowing it to authenticate with MongoDB.  \n\ntool_call:  \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl get deployment geo -n hotel-reservation -o yaml"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 391, 'prompt_tokens': 2810, 'total_tokens': 3201, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb3a-1f5e-7d90-819c-3e8a2dab6ed6-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2810, 'output_tokens': 391, 'total_tokens': 3201}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='2e30fb62-1afe-4509-a2e1-0c2cdb9e4027'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me figure out what to do next. The user is trying to fix the issue with the 'geo' service in their hotel reservation application. So far, they've checked the secrets in the namespace and found that the 'mongodb-geo-auth' Secret was missing. They created it using kubectl apply, and the response was that the secret was created. Now, they need to verify if the deployment for 'geo' is correctly configured to use this new Secret.\n\nThe next step is to check the deployment configuration of the 'geo' service. By retrieving the deployment's YAML, they can see how the Secret is referenced. If the deployment isn't us