sing the Secret, that's a problem. The user should look for sections where the Secret is mounted as a volume or set as an environment variable. \n\nThe tool to use here is 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely' with the command to get the deployment's YAML. This will provide the detailed configuration. Once they have that, they can check if the Secret is properly referenced. If not, they might need to update the deployment to include the Secret. But since the user is in the thinking stage, they need to decide which tool to call next. The correct tool here is 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely' to retrieve the deployment's configuration.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployment geo -n hotel-reservation -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a5bd63da0fc13d0f', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 307, 'prompt_tokens': 3943, 'total_tokens': 4250, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb3a-318c-7e52-aca2-1dbfbeb75a60-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployment geo -n hotel-reservation -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a5bd63da0fc13d0f', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3943, 'output_tokens': 307, 'total_tokens': 4250}), ToolMessage(content='apiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  annotations:\n    deployment.kubernetes.io/revision: "1"\n    kompose.cmd: kompose convert\n    kompose.version: 1.22.0 (955b78124)\n    kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration: |\n      {"apiVersion":"apps/v1","kind":"Deployment","metadata":{"annotations":{"kompose.cmd":"kompose convert","kompose.version":"1.22.0 (955b78124)"},"crea