, MONGO_USER, MONGO_PASS, and MONGO_AUTHDB. But the logs show that MONGO_URI is still not being used. Maybe the application is not reading the MONGO_URI variable, or there's a typo in the variable name. \n\nThe user should verify that the environment variables are correctly set in the pod. They can check the pod's environment variables with 'kubectl exec' to see if the values are present. \n\nAlternatively, the application might be using a different configuration file that's not picking up the environment variables. The logs mention 'cmd/geo/main.go:36' where the database URL is read, so maybe the code is not reading the MONGO_URI variable correctly. \n\nIn any case, the next step is to ensure that the Secret's data is correct and that the environment variables are properly injected into the pod. If the credentials are correct, then the issue might be with the application's configuration or how it's reading the environment variables.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get secret mongodb-geo-auth -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath=\'{.data}\'"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bea91a1e3ff7bef0', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 716, 'prompt_tokens': 11340, 'total_tokens': 12056, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb3d-66ca-7dc0-bde5-b5b1a71a3694-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': "kubectl get secret mongodb-geo-auth -n hotel-reservation -o jsonpath='{.data}'"}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bea91a1e3ff7bef0', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11340, 'output_tokens': 716, 'total_tokens': 12056}), ToolMessage(content='{"authdb":"YWRtaW4