I is still not being used correctly. The app is connecting to mongodb-geo:27017 without the authSource parameter. That suggests the environment variable isn\'t being read properly.\n\nWait, the user tried setting MONGO_URI with the authSource, but the logs show the URI is still missing that part. Maybe the app isn\'t reading the MONGO_URI environment variable at all. Or perhaps the Secret values aren\'t being injected correctly. \n\nThe Secret data was checked earlier, and the username, password, and authdb were present. So the Secret itself is okay. The problem might be in how the Deployment is configured. The env section in the Deployment YAML should correctly reference the Secret keys. Let me check the previous Deployment YAML.\n\nIn the last Deployment update, the env variables MONGO_USER, MONGO_PASS, and MONGO_AUTHDB are set using the Secret. Then, MONGO_URI is constructed using those variables. But if the app isn\'t using MONGO_URI, maybe the code is hardcoding the URI or not reading the environment variable. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the app expects the credentials to be in a different format, like using the username and password directly in the URI without the authSource. But the error message mentions SASL authentication, which typically requires the authSource. \n\nAnother possibility is that the Secret keys are named differently in the app\'s configuration. For example, the app might expect the password to be in a different key, like MONGO_PASSWORD instead of MONGO_PASS. But the user\'s Secret uses MONGO_PASS, which matches the env variable name. \n\nWait, the user\'s Secret has keys username, password, and authdb. The Deployment uses MONGO_USER, MONGO_PASS, and MONGO_AUTHDB. That should map correctly. \n\nHmm, maybe the app is not reading the MONGO_URI at all. The logs show that the app is using the default URI without the authSource. That suggests that the environment variable isn\'t being passed to the app. Could there be a typo in the env variable name