referenced. If that doesn\'t work, the issue might be beyond the user\'s control, and they should submit the answer as is.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \nreasoning: The `geo` pod is still failing to authenticate, and the `MONGO_URI` is not being used by the application. This indicates the app is not reading the `MONGO_URI` environment variable or the Secret values are not correctly injected. To resolve this, we need to explicitly ensure the `MONGO_URI` is correctly formatted with the `authSource` and verify the Secret values are properly referenced.  \n\ntool_call:  \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: geo\\n  namespace: hotel-reservation\\nspec:\\n  template:\\n    spec:\\n      containers:\\n      - name: hotel-reserv-geo\\n        env:\\n        - name: MONGO_URI\\n          value: \\"mongodb://${MONGO_USER}:${MONGO_PASS}@mongodb-geo:27017?authSource=${MONGO_AUTHDB}\\"\\n        - name: MONGO_USER\\n          valueFrom:\\n            secretKeyRef:\\n              name: mongodb-geo-auth\\n              key: username\\n        - name: MONGO_PASS\\n          valueFrom:\\n            secretKeyRef:\\n              name: mongodb-geo-auth\\n              key: password\\n        - name: MONGO_AUTHDB\\n          valueFrom:\\n            secretKeyRef:\\n              name: mongodb-geo-auth\\n              key: authdb\\nEOF"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 2120, 'prompt_tokens': 13346, 'total_tokens': 15466, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb3e-d7eb-7a33-8ee1-b6a733690b87-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 13346, '