ser tried injecting the URI using the Secret values, but it's not working. Maybe the environment variables aren't being set correctly.\n\nWait, the user checked the Secret data and it's there. The Secret has username, password, and authdb. The Deployment YAML references these keys. But when they checked the pod's environment variables, MONGO_URI wasn't present. That means the app isn't reading the MONGO_URI variable. Maybe the app is configured to read the URI from a different source, like a config file or another environment variable.\n\nAlternatively, the app might not be parsing the MONGO_URI correctly. For example, if the app expects the URI in a different format or uses a different method to retrieve the credentials. The error message mentions SASL authentication failure, which usually happens when the username or password is incorrect, or the authSource is missing.\n\nThe user tried setting the MONGO_URI with the authSource, but the logs still show the connection without it. Maybe the app isn't using the URI at all. Perhaps the app is hardcoded to connect to a specific database without using the environment variable. Or the environment variable isn't being passed correctly to the container.\n\nAnother possibility is that the Secret isn't being mounted properly. The user might have a typo in the Secret name or the keys. But the Secret exists and the keys match. So maybe the app is looking for the credentials in a different format, like separate environment variables for username, password, and authSource, instead of a single URI.\n\nIn that case, the app might not be using the MONGO_URI variable. The user should check the app's configuration to see how it's supposed to get the database connection details. If the app expects separate variables for username, password, and authSource, then the MONGO_URI isn't needed. But the logs show the app is trying to connect without the authSource, leading to authentication failure.\n\nSo the solution would be to either adjust the app's configuration to use the correct variables or modify the Deployment to set the necessary environment variables that the app expects. If the app requires separate variables, the user should set those instead of the URI. If the app should use the URI, then the issue is with how the URI is formatted or not being injected correctly.\n\nThe user needs to verify how the geo service is supposed to connect to MongoDB. If the app is using a different method, the environment variables might need to be adjusted accordingly. Alternatively, the app might need to be updated to use the MONGO_URI variable properly.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl rollout restart deployment/geo -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a75a504457621a8b', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 638, 'prompt_tokens': 16623, 'total_tokens': 17261, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb3f-f8cc-7250-a5e6-31cd6d4f2dba-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl rollout restart deployment/geo -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-a75a504457621a8b', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 16623, 'output_tokens': 638, 'total_tokens': 17261}), ToolMessage(content='deployment.apps/geo restarted\n', id='af3e0dca-7311-481a-9905-ac28a808ab0e', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-a75a504457621a8b'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='21b116b8-f04d-40d6-8875-94711f05684c'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s try to fig